## 0. Doors and gates

| Door | Looks like | Needs `/use-mcp` |
|---|---|---|
| Bash CLI | `unity command …`, `unity test …`, `unity open …` | **yes** |
| MCP tools (CLI bridge) | `mcp__unity-editor-mcp__eval`, `…__console`, `…__run_tests` | **yes** |
| MCP tools (in-Editor) | `mcp__unity-mcp__Unity_*` | **retired in <project> (<date>) — never call, even with `/use-mcp`** |
| API reference MCP | `mcp__unity-api__*` | no — offline lookup, touches nothing |
| Bash CLI, read-only diagnostics | `unity status`, `unity doctor`, `unity --version`, `unity pipeline list`, `unity command` (bare list / `--tag`), `unity mcp configure --list` | no — harmless, no Editor mutation |
| Bash CLI, read-only Editor state | `unity command editor_status`, `console_status`, `console` (`--tail`/`--level`), `recompile_status`, `test_status`, `list_tests`, `list_open_scenes` (and their `mcp__unity-editor-mcp__*` twins) | no — read state only, small output |

`unity build`, `unity run`, `unity install`, `unity uninstall`, `unity self-uninstall`,
`unity upgrade` are **never** run by the AI. If one seems needed, say so and stop.

## 1. The bridge follows the running Editor

`unity command` discovers the running Editor itself; it does not follow the chat's directory.
First thing after `/use-mcp`: `unity status --no-banner` — the `Project` column must be this
checkout and the version the one pinned in `CLAUDE.md`. Mismatch → STOP and tell the developer.
No `ready` instance → ask the developer to open the Editor, do not loop.

**Safe Mode:** with compile errors the Pipeline package does not load, so every call reports
"cannot connect" although the Editor is open. Confirm with `unity pipeline list`, read
`Logs/Editor.log` (grep `error CS`), fix on disk, ask the developer to restart Unity.

## 2. Before editing through the bridge

Not in Play mode · not compiling · no modal popup (`editor_status`). After editing `.cs` on
disk: `recompile` → poll `recompile_status` until `completed` / `up_to_date` → read `errors[]`.

## 3. `eval`

A statement list compiled in the Editor: `return <value>;` to get a value back. Fully-qualify
every type (`using` lines do not work). Keep snippets short — heavy logic belongs in a static
method of the project that the snippet calls in one line. Mutations through `eval` bypass Undo;
prefer the dedicated, Undo-aware commands. Never delete files/assets or touch `ProjectSettings/`
through `eval`.

## 4. Tests

`unity command list_tests --mode EditMode` → `run_tests --mode EditMode --filter <name>` → poll
`test_status`. Quote pass/fail counts and failing names, never "tests pass".

## 5. Context discipline

Always `--tail` / `--level error` on `console`; pass `--path` to `get_scene_hierarchy`; save
screenshots with `--save_path` and `Read` the file; write long reports to a file.

## 6. Extending

A static method tagged `[CliCommand]` (asmdef referencing `Unity.Pipeline`) shows up as
`unity command <name>` after the next recompile. `Packages/com.unity.pipeline/` is a third-party
package folder: never edit it; its own `CLAUDE.md` applies only inside that folder.
